From e096a6dd1941ec4ff75f970e99cc27fd811d7166 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Longwei Yang <19267252+Longwei-Yang@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 23:10:34 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 37/41] Safarium: speaker and other alert icons on tabs

Each tab shows Chrome's tab alert (TabAlertController) as an SF Symbol:
playing audio, muted, camera / microphone / screen capture (red),
picture-in-picture, Bluetooth / USB / HID / serial devices, VR. Inactive
tabs show it after the title (sidebar: at the row's trailing edge; pinned
tile: beside the icon); the current tab shows it in the address field left
of reload / page menu. Clicking the speaker mutes or unmutes that tab, as in
Safari; other alerts just select the tab.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
